                        %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+anomaly"} quantum anomaly
                  %div
                    %p
                      %a{:href => "/nlab/edit/differential+cohomology+-+contents"} Edit this sidebar
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connection+on+a+bundle"} connection on a bundle
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connection+on+a+2-bundle"} connection on a 2-bundle
                \/
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connection+on+a+gerbe"} connection on a gerbe
                \/
                %strong connection on a bundle gerbe
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connection+on+a+3-bundle"} connection on a 3-bundle
                \/
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connection+on+a+bundle+2-gerbe"} connection on a bundle 2-gerbe
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connection+on+an+%E2%88%9E-bundle"} connection on an ∞-bundle
          %hr/
          %h1#contents Contents
          .maruku_toc
            %ul
              %li
                %a{:href => "#idea"} Idea
              %ul
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#definitions"} Definitions
                %ul
                  %li
                    %a{:href => "#for_line_bundle_gerbes"} For line bundle gerbes
                  %li
                    %a{:href => "#for_principal_bundle_gerbes"} For principal bundle gerbes
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#surface_transport"} Surface transport
              %li
                %a{:href => "#related_concepts"} Related concepts
              %li
                %a{:href => "#further_references"} Further references
          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %em
              connection on a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bundle+gerbe"} bundle gerbe
            is a slight variant of a
            = succeed "-realization" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cech+cohomology"} Cech
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Deligne+cohomology"} Deligne cohomology
            cocycle.
          %blockquote
            %p old content, needs to be polished
          %p
            Like a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connection+on+a+bundle"} connection
            on a locally trivialized bundle is encoded in a Lie algebra-valued connection
            = succeed "-form" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            = succeed "-form" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            (this shift in degree is directly related to the step from second to third integral cohomology). This
            = succeed "-form" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2
            %em
              curving
              = succeed "-form" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2
            of a bundle gerbe.
          %p
            But there is more data necessary to describe a connection on a bundle gerbe. The details of the definition – which is evident for line bundle gerbes but more involved for principal bundle gerbes – can be naturally derived from a functorial concept of parallel surface transport, just like connection
            = succeed "-forms" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
          %h3#definitions Definitions
          %h4#for_line_bundle_gerbes For line bundle gerbes
          %p A connection (also known as “connection and curving”) on a line bundle gerbe
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mi p
                  %msup
                    %mi Y
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mo →
                  %mi Y
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mi π
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  B \stackrel{p}{\to} Y^{[2]} \stackrel{\to}{\to} Y \stackrel{\pi}{\to} X
          %p is
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                a 2-form on
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi B
                      %mo ∈
                      %msup
                        %mi Ω
                        %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      B \in \Omega^2(Y)
            %li
              %p
                a connection
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo ∇
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nabla
                on the line bundle
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi B
                      %mo →
                      %msup
                        %mi Y
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mn 2
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B \to Y^{[2]}
            %li
              %p such that
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msubsup
                        %mi π
                        %mn 1
                        %mo *
                      %mi B
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo −
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %msubsup
                        %mi p
                        %mn 2
                        %mo *
                      %mi B
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo =
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %msub
                        %mi F
                        %mo ∇
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\pi_1^*B \; -\;  p_2^*B \;=\; F_\nabla
            %li
              %p
                together with an extension of the bundle gerbe product
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi μ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu
                to an isomorphism
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi μ
                        %mo ∇
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo :
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %msubsup
                        %mi p
                        %mn 12
                        %mo *
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi B
                      %mo ,
                      %mo ∇
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo ⊗
                      %msubsup
                        %mi p
                        %mn 23
                        %mo *
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi B
                      %mo ,
                      %mo ∇
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo →
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %msubsup
                        %mi p
                        %mn 13
                        %mo *
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi B
                      %mo ,
                      %mo ∇
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\mu_\nabla \;:\; p_{12}^* (B,\nabla) \;\; \otimes p_{23}^* (B,\nabla) \;\to\; p_{13}^* (B,\nabla)
              %p of line bundles with connection.
          %p
            Notice that this condition ensures that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi d
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d B
            is a
            = succeed "-form" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 3
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 3
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            which agrees on double intersections
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi p
                    %mn 1
                    %mo *
                  %mi d
                  %mi B
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo =
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msubsup
                    %mi p
                    %mn 2
                    %mo *
                  %mi d
                  %mi B
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  p_1^* d B \;\; = \;\; p_2^* d B
                  \\,.
          %p
            This means that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi d
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d B
            actually descends to a 3-form on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %p
            The
            %strong curvature
            associated with the connection on a line bundle gerbe is the unique 3-form on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi H
                  %mo ∈
                  %msup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mn 3
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  H \in \Omega^3(X)
          %p such that
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi π
                    %mo *
                  %mi H
                  %mo =
                  %mi d
                  %mi B
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\pi^* H = d B
                  \\,.
          %p
            The deRham class
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [H]
            of this 3-form is the image in real cohomology of the class in integral coholomology classifying the bundle gerbe.
          %h4#for_principal_bundle_gerbes For principal bundle gerbes
          %p
            A connection on a
            = succeed "-principal" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                a
                = succeed "-valued" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Lie
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi G
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{Lie}(G)
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi B
                      %mo ∈
                      %msup
                        %mi Ω
                        %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Y
                      %mo ,
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Lie
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi G
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      B \in \Omega^2(Y,\mathrm{Lie}(G))
            %li
              %p
                together with a
                = succeed "-valued" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Lie
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Aut
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi G
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{Lie}(\mathrm{Aut}(G))
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo ∈
                      %msup
                        %mi Ω
                        %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Y
                      %mo ,
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Lie
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Aut
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi G
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      A \in \Omega^1(Y,\mathrm{Lie}(\mathrm{Aut}(G)))
            %li
              %p
                and a certain twisted notion of connection on the
                = succeed "-bundle" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi G
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            %li
              %p
                satisfying a couple of conditions that reduce to those described above in the case
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi G
                        %mo =
                        %mi U
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G = U(1)
          %p
            For the case that
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi F
                      %mi A
                    %mo +
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} ad
                    %mi B
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F_{A} + \mathrm{ad} B = 0
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            to the category
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi G
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} BiTor
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma(G\mathrm{BiTor})
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math.DG/0511710"} math.DG/0511710
          %p
            For the more general case a choice for these conditions that harmonizes with the conditions found for (proper) gerbes with connection by Breen &amp; Messing in
            %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math.AG/0106083"} math.AG/0106083
            has been given by Aschieri, Cantini &amp; Jurčo in
            %br/
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0312154"} hep-th/0312154
          %h3#surface_transport Surface transport
          %p
            From a line bundle gerbe with connection one obtains a notion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/parallel+transport"} parallel transport
            along surfaces in a way that generalizes the procedure for locally trivialized fiber bundles with connection.
          %p
            Recall that in the case of fiber bundles, the holonomy associated to a based loop
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi γ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \gamma
            is obtained by
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                choosing a triangulation of the loop (i.e., a decomposition into intervals) such that each vertex sits in a double intersection
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mi ij
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_{ij}
                and such that each edge sits in a patch
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mi i
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_i
            %li
              %p
                choosing for each edge a lift into
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Y
                      %mo =
                      %msub
                        %mo ⊔
                        %mi i
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mi i
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y = \sqcup_i U_i
            %li
              %p
                choosing for each vertex a lift into
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi Y
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mn 2
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo =
                      %msub
                        %mo ⊔
                        %mi ij
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mi i
                      %mo ∩
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mi j
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y^{[2]} = \sqcup_{ij} U_i\cap U_j
            %li
              %p
                assigning to each edge lifted to
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mi i
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_i
                the transport computed from the connection 1-form
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi a
                        %mi i
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a_i
            %li
              %p
                assigning to each vertex lifted to
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mi i
                      %mo ∩
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mi j
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_i \cap U_j
                the value of the transition function
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi g
                        %mi ij
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g_{ij}
                at that point
            %li
              %p
                multiplying these data in the order given by
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi γ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \gamma
                \.
          %p
            For bundle gerbes this generalizes to a procedure that assigns a triangulation to a closed surface, that lifts faces, edges, and vertices to single, double and triple intersections, respectively, and which assigns the exponentiated integrals of the 2-form over faces, of the connection 1-form over edges, and assigns the isomorphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi μ
                    %mi ijk
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu_{ijk}
            to vertices.
          %p For the abelian case (line bundle gerbes) this procedure has been first described in
          %ul
            %li
              K. Gawedzki &amp; N. Reis,
              %em WZW branes and Gerbes
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0205233"}> arXiv
              )
          %p based on
          %ul
            %li
              O. Alvarez,
              %em Topological quantization and cohomology
              Commun. Math. Phys. 100 (1985), 279-309.
          %p Further discussion can be found in
          %ul
            %li
              A. Carey, S. Johnson &amp; M. Murray,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Holonomy on D-branes
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0204199"} arXiv
          %p Gawedzki and Reis showed this way that the Wess-Zumino term in the WZW-model is nothing but the surface holonomy of a (line bundle) gerbe.
          %p
            In terms of string physics this means that the string (the
            = succeed "-particle)" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2
            = succeed "-)particle" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
          %p The necessity to interpret the Kalb–Ramond field as a connection on a gerbe was originally discussed in
          %ul
            %li
              D. Freed and E. Witten
              = succeed "," do
                %em Anomalies in string theory with D-branes
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9907189"} arXiv
          %p
            Underlying the Gawedzki–Reis formula is a general mechanism of transition of transport
            = succeed "-functors," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"}> Urs Schreiber
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Konrad+Waldorf"} Konrad Waldorf
              = succeed "," do
                %em Connections on non-abelian gerbes and their holonomy
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://www.tac.mta.ca/tac/volumes/28/17/28-17abs.html"} TAC
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0808.1923"} arXiv:0808.1923
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://ncatlab.org/schreiber/show/differential+cohomology+in+an+(%E2%88%9E%2C1)-topos+--+references#SchrWalII+III"} web
          %p and similarly in
          %ul
            %li
              Joao Faria Martins, Roger Picken,
              %em A Cubical Set Approach to 2-Bundles with Connection and Wilson Surfaces
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0808.3964"}> arXiv
              )
          %p This applies to more general situations than ordinary line bundle gerbes with connection.
          %p
            The generalization (“
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jandl+gerbes"}> Jandl gerbes
            ”) to unoriented surfaces (hence to type I strings)
          %ul
            %li
              K. Waldorf, C. Schweigert &amp; U. S.,
              %em Unoriented WZW Models and Holonomy of Bundle Gerbes
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0512283"}> arXiv
              )
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/B-field"} B-field
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Deligne+cohomology"} Deligne cohomology
          %h2#further_references Further references
          %p (…)
          %p
            In relation to
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordinary+differential+cohomology"} ordinary differential cohomology
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Byungdo+Park"}> Byungdo Park
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Differential cohomology and gerbes: An introduction to higher differential geometry
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://byungdo.github.io/seminars/IMSRS.pdf"} pdf
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Park-DifferentialCohomology.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
          %p
            Discussion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/transgression"} transgression
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+holonomy"} higher holonomy
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Deligne+cohomology"} Deligne cohomology
            (for
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bundle+gerbes+with+connection"} bundle gerbes with connection
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orbifolds"} orbifolds
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ernesto+Lupercio"}> Ernesto Lupercio
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bernardo+Uribe"} Bernardo Uribe
              = succeed "," do
                %em Holonomy for Gerbes over Orbifolds
              %strong 56
              (2006) 1534-1560 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/math/0307114"}> arXiv:math/0307114
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.geomphys.2005.08.006"} doi:10.1016/j.geomphys.2005.08.006
